    "datePosted": "2026-11-20T08:17:20.000Z",
    "description": "Position Regional Capacity Building Advisor Project EU CSF+: Enhancing the role and participation of CSOs in promoting good governance and ensuring inclusive development in Ethiopia Duty station Afar Area Office, Semera Number of positions 1 Reports to Project Coordinator Salary Based on DEC's salary scale Closing date 28 November 2026 About DEC Development Expertise Center (DEC) is a national civil society organization established in 2007 and re-registered in May 2019 under the Authority for Civil Society Organizations Proclamation (registration number 0009). DEC runs five programs: Child Well-being and Education Development, Gender and Life Skills Development, Employable Skills Development, Advocacy, and Humanitarian Emergency. We work in Amhara, Afar, Oromia, Tigray, Gambela, Benishangul Gumuz, South West Ethiopia, and Addis Ababa City Administration. About the project The EU CSF+: Enhancing the role and participation of CSOs in promoting good governance and ensuring inclusive development in Ethiopia is a five-year (2023 to 2027) program funded by the European Union. It aims to help local and grassroots civil society organizations (CSOs) in Ethiopia become active, accountable actors in governance and development. It builds on the progress of the earlier EU Civil Society Fund and on the current reform momentum for CSOs. The program works through three main strategies: Capacity building for local and grassroots CSOs, associations and networks, covering technical, financial and organizational skills, evidence-based policy advocacy, and the rights-based approach. Financial support through sub-granting, so CSOs can manage funds and implement actions well. A better enabling environment for civil society, including stronger partnerships, knowledge exchange, social cohesion, peaceful transformation, and closer engagement with government. The program is strengthening local and grassroots CSOs, associations and networks. About the role The Regional Capacity Building Advisor will be based in Semera and will support CSOs in the Afar region. The advisor will lead their organizational development and systems strengthening, design and deliver tailored capacity-building activities, and follow each partner's progress to make sure activities are delivered on time and meet quality standards. Key responsibilities Help target CSOs in the region, and assess their capacity needs. Collect, document and manage data on all target CSOs in the region. Design and deliver tailored training, coaching and mentoring for partner CSOs. Support CSOs in organizational development, systems strengthening and compliance with relevant government regulations. Provide ongoing technical support to partner CSOs on organizational systems, project implementation and reporting. Track the progress of each CSO against its capacity-building plan. Support the Project Coordinator in planning, implementing and monitoring project activities. Prepare quarterly, biannual and annual work plans and reports and submit them to the Project Coordinator. Compile and review the reports of partner CSOs, give feedback for improvement, and share the consolidated reports with the project team Monitor partners to ensure timely implementation and that quality standards are met. Work closely with CSOs, local authorities, government stakeholders and the project team, and build strong working relationships with them. Maintain frequent communication and cooperation with stakeholders and partners to define project requirements, scope and objectives Build and maintain partnerships with target CSOs and like-minded organizations. Document best practices with the DEC and partner PMEL units and share them with relevant bodies. Contribute to proposal development, project revisions and amendments as needed. Carry out other tasks assigned by the Project Coordinator, the Program Coordinator or DEC's Senior Management Team.",
