    "description": "Job Title: IYCF Officer Duty Station: Afar Region – Afambo/Amibara Reports to: Project Coordinator Employment Type: Full-time No of vacant post: Two Deadline: November 24, 2026 Organizational Overview Nexus Ethiopia is a national Ethiopian Civil Society Organization committed to strengthening the resilience of vulnerable and crisis-affected communities through integrated Humanitarian–Development–Peace (HDP) Nexus programming, localization, partnership, and locally led humanitarian action. Nexus Ethiopia, in partnership with other humanitarian actors, is implementing project entitled Integrated Lifesaving Humanitarian Response for Drought, Flood and Displacement-Affected Communities in Afambo and Amibara Woredas, Afar Region. Project Background The project is a multisectoral humanitarian response designed to provide lifesaving assistance and protection to drought-, flood- and displacement-affected communities in Afar Region, Afambo and Amibara woredas. The role supports Nexus Ethiopia’s health and nutrition implementation team and works with government health services, community structures and other project sectors. Job Purpose Lead infant and young child feeding in emergencies (IYCF-E) activities in Afambo and Amibara. Improve access to practical, respectful feeding support for pregnant and lactating women and caregivers of children under two, and link families with nutrition, health and other relevant services. Key Responsibilities IYCF planning and service delivery Prepare monthly IYCF-E workplans and activity budgets with the Project Coordinator, Nutrition Officer and woreda counterparts. Assess caregiver needs, feeding practices and barriers to service access through consultations and routine service contacts. Provide individual and group counselling on breastfeeding, age-appropriate complementary feeding and maternal nutrition using approved materials. Support caregivers facing feeding difficulties within professional competence and refer cases requiring specialized assessment or care. Adapt outreach schedules and communication to pastoral mobility, displacement, literacy and local language needs. Community support and capacity development Establish or strengthen mother-to-mother and caregiver support groups with community representatives and Health Extension Workers. Coach facility staff, outreach teams and community volunteers on counselling skills, respectful engagement and appropriate referral. Develop session plans and practical demonstrations using locally appropriate foods and approved counselling materials. Engage fathers and other caregivers to support feeding and care practices, while ensuring privacy and voluntary participation. Integration quality and referrals Coordinate with the Nutrition Officer to link feeding support with screening, treatment follow-up and referral for malnutrition. Work with health teams to integrate IYCF counselling into antenatal, postnatal, child health and mobile outreach services. Coordinate hygiene messages and safe food preparation practices with WASH staff. Promote responsible management of breast-milk substitutes in line with applicable guidance and refer any proposed distribution to the designated technical lead. Observe counselling sessions, obtain caregiver feedback and provide corrective coaching to improve service quality. Monitoring accountability and reporting Maintain confidential counselling, group-session and referral records, distinguishing unique caregivers from repeat contacts. Submit timely activity reports and indicator updates to the Project Coordinator and MEAL team, including service gaps and proposed actions. Track referral completion and caregiver follow-up in collaboration with nutrition and health teams. Ensure women, adolescent mothers and caregivers with disabilities can access services and feedback channels safely. Apply safeguarding, PSEA, confidentiality and informed-consent practices; report concerns through designated channels.",
