    "description": "Position Overview / Scope of Role The Electro-Mechanical Technician is responsible for installing, inspecting, maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing electrical and mechanical systems, machinery, and equipment used in construction operations. The role ensures the reliable operation, safety, and efficiency of electromechanical equipment through preventive maintenance, timely breakdown response, technical inspections, and proper repair practices. The position also provides technical support to construction teams and ensures that equipment and systems remain operational to support uninterrupted project execution. Top Roles and Responsibilities Electro-Mechanical Installation and Maintenance Install, inspect, maintain, and repair electrical and mechanical components, equipment, and systems. Carry out installation, connection, testing, and commissioning of electromechanical equipment in accordance with technical specifications and safety requirements. Maintain electrical motors, pumps, generators, compressors, lifting equipment, and other construction-related machinery. Inspect electrical panels, control systems, wiring, switches, circuit breakers, and mechanical drive components. Perform routine servicing, lubrication, adjustment, and replacement of worn or damaged components. Ensure proper functioning and operational readiness of assigned equipment and systems. Troubleshooting and Breakdown Management Diagnose electrical, mechanical, and electromechanical faults using appropriate tools and testing equipment. Identify the root causes of equipment failures and implement appropriate repair solutions. Respond promptly to equipment breakdowns to minimize operational interruptions. Repair or replace defective electrical components, motors, bearings, pumps, cables, control devices, and mechanical parts. Conduct functional tests after repairs to ensure equipment is safe and operational. Recommend corrective measures to prevent recurring equipment failures. Preventive Maintenance and Equipment Reliability Implement scheduled preventive maintenance plans for machinery, equipment, and electromechanical installations. Conduct regular inspections to identify abnormal operating conditions, overheating, vibration, leakage, electrical faults, and mechanical wear. Maintain equipment maintenance records, service histories, and inspection reports. Identify maintenance requirements and communicate spare parts, tools, and material needs to the responsible supervisor. Recommend improvements to increase equipment reliability, operational efficiency, and service life. Construction Equipment and Site Technical Support Provide technical maintenance and repair support for construction machinery and equipment. Coordinate with site engineers, equipment operators, and construction teams to identify equipment maintenance requirements. Support the installation, relocation, and operational setup of electromechanical equipment at construction sites. Inspect electrical and mechanical systems associated with construction facilities and temporary site installations. Ensure equipment is maintained in accordance with operational and safety requirements. Technical Coordination Coordinate maintenance and repair activities with relevant technical and construction personnel. Monitor the quality of maintenance work and ensure that completed repairs meet technical requirements. Provide technical guidance and practical support to junior technicians and assigned maintenance personnel. Support the development of practical maintenance procedures and technical working standards. Safety and Compliance Ensure all electrical and mechanical maintenance activities comply with occupational health and safety requirements. Apply appropriate electrical isolation, lockout, and equipment shutdown procedures before maintenance work. Use appropriate testing instruments, tools, and personal protective equipment. Identify and report electrical hazards, mechanical risks, and unsafe equipment conditions. Maintain an organized workshop and work area and ensure proper handling of tools and maintenance materials. Documentation and Reporting Prepare maintenance reports covering inspections, repairs, breakdowns, and preventive maintenance activities. Maintain accurate records of equipment conditions, service history, spare parts usage, and outstanding maintenance requirements. Report major technical problems and recommend appropriate solutions to the immediate supervisor. Provide updates on equipment availability, maintenance progress, and recurring technical issues. Perform other related duties as directed.",
