    "description": "Human Rights Officer, Disabilities and Older Person Rights Human Rights Monitoring Internal/External Announcement About Human Rights Monitoring Purpose of the Job: Conduct the day-to-day monitoring activities related to Human Rights in the different sectors and at different levels, for the promotion and protection of Persons with disabilities and older persons rights. Main Duties and Responsibilities: Serve as the monitoring focal point for assigned monitoring activities relating to persons with disabilities and older persons, and ensure that these rights are mainstreamed in all EHRC monitoring units, departments, and city offices. Contribute to the development of monitoring tools and methodologies, and reports across all EHRC departments and city offices integrate the rights and perspectives of persons with disabilities and older persons. Provide technical inputs, as requested, to other departments and city offices on monitoring the rights of persons with disabilities and older persons. Contribute to the design and implementation of strategies aiming at enhanced promotion and protection of Persons with disabilities and older persons rights through regular and continuous monitoring and reporting; Conduct monitoring on selected institutions to assess whether their policies and procedures are in compliance with international and regional human rights standards and produce reports with concrete remedial recommendations. Conduct fact-finding missions on human rights abuses, including systemic violations affecting persons with disabilities and older persons, in close cooperation with relevant stakeholders, human rights actors, and communities. Contribute to and/or draft monitoring reports, advocacy briefs, communications, briefing notes, statements, and other products; Monitor the situation of persons with disabilities and older persons during exceptional circumstances (elections, conflict, emergencies, displacement, public health crises, climate events). Apply accessibility standards in all assigned monitoring activities, tools, and venues. Assist in conducting capacity-building activities and in developing and implementing training programs on the rights of persons with disabilities and older persons; Contribute to the mainstreaming of the rights of persons with disabilities and older persons in other EHRC activities and programming, and integrate gender perspectives in all activities of the Unit; Conduct mapping of stakeholders and set up referral system to provide support to persons with disabilities and older persons who suffered human rights violation and are in need of support; Follow up on the implementation of EHRC recommendations, and of recommendations, general comments, and concluding observations of international and regional human rights bodies relevant to the rights of persons with disabilities and older persons, and update the recommendation tracking records; Establish and maintain contact with technical staff of government and non-governmental institutions, civil society organizations, UN agencies, the private sector, development partners, and other partners working on persons with disabilities and older persons; Participate in discussion forums with institutions and organizations, including other NHRIs, for joint programming and the sharing of experience and promising practices; Provide technical information and guidance to requesting groups, communities, and victims on the rights of persons with disabilities and older persons., and refer them to the appropriate EHRC departments or service providers; Ensure that every operation and activity adheres to legal guidelines, internal policies of EHRC, and international and regional human rights standards; Keep the Coordinator informed through regular, detailed, and accurate reports on progress and challenges in the monitoring, campaign and advocacy work conducted by the Unit; Perform additional assignments and delegations given by the Coordinator.",
