    "description": "Job Title : Certification, Compliance and Traceability Officer Duty Station: Head Office, Addis Ababa, with frequent travel to farms and processing facilities. Reports to : Group Supply Chain, Quality, and Certification Director Employment Type : Full time About Moyee Coffee Moyee Coffee Roasting Plc is the first multinational coffee roasting company based in Ethiopia and a pioneer of the FairChain movement. As a fully integrated company from crop to cup we handle the entire value chain from growing to roasting coffee locally. We export premium roasted coffee to international markets and supply top-tier hotels and leading supermarkets across Ethiopia, ensuring maximum value remains at origin. 1. Position purpose The Certification, Compliance and Traceability Officer is responsible for planning, implementing, coordinating and maintaining all relevant national and international certification systems, sustainability standards, food safety requirements and export compliance procedures across the Group's agricultural and coffee businesses. The officer will oversee and ensure compliance of all farms, coffee sourcing operations, processing facilities, export cleaning facilities, warehouses, and roasting and packaging facilities with applicable certification standards and regulatory requirements. These include EUDR, Organic Certification, Rainforest Alliance, JAS, and other relevant food safety, sustainability, and quality management standards, such as ISO and HACCP. The position will establish an integrated certification and traceability system that supports regulatory compliance, market access, sustainable production, product integrity and international buyer confidence. 2. Companies and facilities under responsibility The officer will coordinate certification and compliance activities of Tega Tula Farm, Exchange, Moye Coffee, and other company farms under establishment. The responsibility of officer extends across own farm production, out grower farmers, washing stations, export processing and roasting facilities under the group businesses. Key Responsibilities A. EUDR Compliance and Supply Chain Traceability Coordinate and oversee the implementation of EUDR requirements, ensuring farm level traceability, geolocation mapping, deforestation risk assessment, due diligence, and accurate documentation across the entire coffee supply chain, from farm to export. B. Organic Certification Management Manage and maintain organic certification programs across coffee farms, processing facilities, and supply chain operations. Ensure compliance with applicable organic standards, coordinate inspections and audits, monitor corrective actions, and maintain proper certification and traceability records. C. Rainforest Alliance Certification Management Coordinate the implementation and continuous compliance of Rainforest Alliance certification requirements. Oversee farm and supply chain compliance assessments, internal inspections, audit preparation, farmer training, sustainability practices, and corrective action follow up. D. Food Safety and Processing Facility Certifications (HACCP, ISO 22000, GMP, etc.) Coordinate the development, implementation, and maintenance of food safety management systems and relevant processing facility certifications. Ensure compliance with food safety, hygiene, quality control, and operational standards across coffee processing, warehousing, roasting, and packaging facilities. Oversee internal audits, risk assessments, corrective actions, and continuous improvement initiatives. Reporting and working relationships The officer will report directly to the Group Supply Chain, Quality, and Certification Director and work closely with Farm Managers and Agronomists, as well as teams responsible for coffee procurement and supply chain, processing, quality control, export, warehousing and inventory management, roasting, and packaging.",
