    "description": "JOB DESCRIPTION TALENT OFFICER Job Title Talent Officer Department Talent Reports To Talent Director 1. Job Purpose The Talent Officer supports the effective implementation of EIH’s talent management priorities by coordinating talent acquisition, performance management, learning and development, talent development, employee engagement, and related HR services. The role works closely with the Talent Director, department heads, employees, and external service providers to ensure that talent processes are delivered efficiently, consistently, and in alignment with EIH’s strategic objectives, policies, and procedures. 2. Key Duties and Responsibilities A. Talent Acquisition and Employer Branding Coordinate recruitment activities in consultation with the Talent Director and hiring departments, including preparation of vacancy announcements, job descriptions, candidate screening, interview schedules, assessments, and selection documentation. Source and identify potential candidates through appropriate recruitment channels, professional networks, recruitment agencies, universities, and other relevant platforms. Maintain accurate recruitment records, candidate databases, and talent pipelines to support current and anticipated workforce requirements. Support employer branding initiatives, career events, job fairs, and professional outreach activities to strengthen EIH’s visibility as an employer of choice. Coordinate reference checks, pre-employment documentation, and recruitment-related communication in accordance with EIH procedures. B. Onboarding and Employee Lifecycle Support Coordinate onboarding and induction arrangements for new employees, ensuring timely completion of required documentation and orientation activities. Facilitate employee movement processes, including appointments, transfers, promotions, acting assignments, contract renewals, and separations, and maintain the related records. Maintain and regularly update employee files and HR master data in both electronic and physical formats, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and confidentiality. Coordinate the preparation and submission of monthly payroll inputs and employee movement information to Finance and other relevant units. Provide first-line support to employees on routine HR matters and refer complex or sensitive cases to the Talent Director. C. Performance Management Coordinate the annual performance management cycle, including objective setting, KPI documentation, periodic reviews, year-end assessments, and performance records. Work with departments and employees to facilitate the alignment of individual objectives and KPIs with approved departmental and corporate objectives. Monitor completion of performance management activities and follow up with departments to ensure adherence to approved timelines and procedures. Support the coordination of performance review discussions, feedback processes, and documentation of performance outcomes. Compile performance management data and reports, identify implementation gaps, and escalate issues and recommendations to the Talent Director. D. Learning and Development Coordinate the identification and consolidation of employee learning and development needs in collaboration with department heads and employees. Support the preparation and implementation of the annual learning and development plan in line with EIH’s strategic priorities, competency requirements, and available resources. Organize internal and external training programs, workshops, knowledge-sharing sessions, and other learning interventions. Coordinate training nominations, approvals, logistics, attendance records, provider engagement, and post-training evaluations. Maintain learning and development records and monitor the implementation of individual development plans and agreed learning actions. Support the evaluation of learning effectiveness and prepare reports on participation, completion, feedback, and identified development outcomes. E. Talent Development and Succession Planning Support the identification of critical positions, talent development needs, and potential successors in collaboration with the Talent Director and relevant department heads. Coordinate the documentation and periodic updating of succession plans, talent profiles, and individual development actions. Support the implementation of career development, coaching, mentoring, and other talent development initiatives. Maintain records of talent reviews and follow up on agreed development actions, escalating implementation gaps where necessary. F. Employee Engagement, Retention and HR Services Coordinate employee engagement activities, internal communication initiatives, staff learning events, recognition activities, and other approved culture-building programs. Support the administration of employee feedback and engagement surveys and assist in consolidating findings and tracking agreed actions. Coordinate routine employee welfare and benefits administration, including medical insurance enrollment, updates for joiners and leavers, claims follow-up, and liaison with service providers. Maintain leave records and coordinate leave administration in line with EIH policies and procedures. Support the implementation and communication of employee retention initiatives and escalate recurring employee concerns or service issues to the Talent Director. G. HR Reporting, Compliance and Coordination Prepare periodic HR and talent reports, dashboards, and data summaries covering recruitment, headcount, employee movements, performance, learning, engagement, and other relevant indicators. Maintain accurate and up-to-date HR documentation, trackers, databases, and records to support timely reporting and informed decision-making. Support the implementation of Talent policies, procedures, guidelines, and approved initiatives, and promote consistent application across the organization. Handle employee and organizational information with strict confidentiality, professionalism, and discretion. Coordinate with internal departments and external stakeholders, including recruitment agencies, training providers, insurance companies, banks, government institutions, and relevant SOE HR teams, as required. Provide coordination support to SOEs and new investments on transitional talent management needs when assigned. Undertake other related duties assigned by the immediate supervisor.",
