    "description": "The Financial Operations Manager is responsible for overseeing and managing the company's day to day financial operations, ensuring accuracy, efficiency, transparency, and compliance with established financial policies and procedures. The role focuses on managing financial transactions, payment processing, reconciliations, cash flow monitoring, financial controls, and operational reporting. The position ensures effective coordination between Finance, Operations, Customer Service, Technology, and other departments to support smooth business operations and maintain the financial integrity of the company's products and services. Key Responsibilities A. Financial Operations Management Oversee daily financial operations and ensure the accuracy and efficiency of financial activities. Manage and monitor financial transactions, payment processing, settlements, and related operational activities. Ensure proper recording, verification, and documentation of financial transactions. Develop and implement effective financial operational procedures and workflows. Monitor financial activities to identify operational gaps, inefficiencies, and potential risks. Ensure timely execution of financial transactions and operational commitments. B. Financial Reconciliation and Transaction Management Oversee daily, weekly, and monthly financial reconciliations. Ensure accurate reconciliation of bank accounts, payment channels, digital transactions, and internal financial records. Investigate transaction discrepancies, failed transactions, duplicate payments, and settlement differences. Coordinate with banks, payment service providers, and business partners to resolve financial transaction issues. Ensure proper tracking and resolution of outstanding transactions and financial discrepancies. Maintain accurate reconciliation records and supporting documentation. C. Cash Flow and Treasury Operations Monitor daily cash positions and liquidity requirements. Coordinate cash flow monitoring and short-term financial planning. Ensure sufficient funds are available to support operational and business requirements. Monitor incoming and outgoing payments and ensure timely settlements. Coordinate with financial institutions regarding cash management and banking operations. Identify potential liquidity challenges and escalate them to the Finance Director. D. Financial Controls and Risk Management Implement and monitor internal financial controls to safeguard company assets. Ensure proper authorization and approval of financial transactions. Identify and assess financial operational risks and recommend appropriate control measures. Monitor compliance with internal financial policies, procedures, and applicable regulatory requirements. Prevent and identify irregular transactions, financial discrepancies, and potential fraudulent activities. Ensure proper segregation of financial duties and responsibilities. E. Financial Reporting and Performance Monitoring Prepare and review daily, weekly, and monthly financial operational reports. Monitor transaction volumes, settlement performance, reconciliation status, and operational efficiency. Provide management with accurate financial operational information for decision-making. Analyze financial operational performance and identify areas for improvement. Develop and monitor relevant financial operations KPIs. Ensure timely submission of financial operational reports to the Finance Director. F. Digital Financial Services and Payment Operations Oversee the operational financial processes supporting the company's digital financial products and services. Coordinate financial transaction operations with Technology, Operations, and Customer Service teams. Monitor digital payment transactions, wallet activities, transaction settlements, and related financial records. Ensure proper handling and resolution of transaction-related complaints and financial discrepancies. Collaborate with the Technology team to improve financial transaction processes and system reliability. Support the implementation and improvement of automated financial operations and reporting systems. G. Team and Cross-Departmental Coordination Supervise, guide, and evaluate the performance of the Financial Operations team. Assign responsibilities and ensure effective execution of daily financial activities. Establish clear operational procedures and accountability within the team. Coordinate with Finance, Operations, Customer Service, Technology, and other departments. Provide operational guidance and training to relevant employees. Ensure effective communication and timely resolution of cross-departmental financial issues.",
