    "description": "INTERNAL /EXTERNANAL VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT FOR THE POSTION OF GBV OFFICER Vacancy post date: 19/11/2026 Project: Survivor-Centered Protection and GBV Services for Conflict-Affected Women and Girls in East Belesa and Dabat Woredas Duty Station: Amhara Region, North Gondar Zone Dabat Woreda Employment Type: Project-Based Contract (Five Months) Number of Positions: One (1) Organizational Background Development through Adult and Non-Formal Education (DANFE) is a local civil society organization established in 2004 by volunteers committed to supporting vulnerable communities. DANFE implements humanitarian and development interventions, including survivor-centered protection and gender-based violence (GBV) response, emergency education, support for internally displaced persons, women's economic empowerment, climate-resilient livelihoods, peace building and conflict prevention. About the Position Development through Adult and Non-Formal Education (DANFE) seeks a qualified and motivated GBV Officer to support the implementation of a survivor-centered protection and GBV response project for conflict-affected women and girls. The position will be responsible for coordinating GBV prevention, risk mitigation, case management oversight, referral services, community engagement, and Women and Girls Friendly Space (WGFS) activities. Key Responsibilities Provide technical oversight and support to GBV caseworkers and volunteers. Ensure quality, confidential, and survivor-centered GBV case management services. Plan and implement GBV prevention, awareness-raising, and risk mitigation activities. Coordinate and strengthen Women and Girls Friendly Spaces (WGFS). Strengthen referral pathways and coordinate with service providers and stakeholders. Support community-based protection mechanisms and capacity-building initiatives. Prepare project reports and ensure compliance with safeguarding and PSEA standards. Major Duties and Responsibilities A. GBV Case Management and Survivor Support Provide technical oversight and guidance to GBV caseworkers to ensure quality, timely and survivor-centered case management. Ensure that GBV survivors have access to safe identification, intake, needs and risk assessment, safety planning, referral, follow-up and case closure services. Monitor the quality of case management documentation and ensure secure handling and storage of confidential information. Ensure survivors receive appropriate and timely referrals to clinical management, psychosocial support, legal assistance, protection and other essential services. Support the management of complex and high-risk cases through appropriate technical consultation and safe referral mechanisms. Ensure informed consent, confidentiality, non-discrimination, respect and survivor autonomy throughout service delivery. B. GBV Prevention and Risk Mitigation Plan and implement community-based GBV prevention and awareness-raising activities targeting women, girls, men, boys and community stakeholders. Identify and monitor GBV risks affecting women and girls in communities, service delivery locations, schools, health facilities, water points and humanitarian distribution sites. Conduct or facilitate protection risk assessments and safety audits and recommend appropriate mitigation measures. Integrate GBV risk mitigation into dignity kit distributions, cash assistance, community mobilization and other project interventions. Promote women's and girls' participation in identifying protection concerns and developing community-based solutions. Support initiatives addressing harmful gender norms, discrimination, exploitation and other factors contributing to GBV. C. Women and Girls Friendly Space (WGFS) Management Coordinate the establishment, rehabilitation, operationalization and effective utilization of Women and Girls Friendly Spaces. Ensure that WGFS provide safe, inclusive, accessible and confidential environments for women and girls. Organize structured recreational, awareness, life-skills and psychosocial support activities in collaboration with relevant project staff. Ensure the availability and proper management of WGFS materials, supplies, equipment and activity schedules. Monitor service utilization and identify gaps affecting the quality, accessibility and sustainability of WGFS services. Strengthen community participation and ownership in the management and protection of WGFS. D. Referral Pathway and Stakeholder Coordination Strengthen and maintain functional GBV referral pathways in collaboration with health facilities, women and social affairs offices, police, justice institutions and other relevant service providers. Coordinate with MHPSS, child protection, health and protection teams to ensure integrated and timely service provision. Facilitate coordination meetings, case-related technical consultations and referral follow-ups while maintaining confidentiality. Strengthen the capacity and engagement of community protection structures, including community protection committees and relevant women's groups. Maintain updated service directories and referral information for the project operational areas. Represent DANFE in relevant GBV coordination, protection and humanitarian response meetings as assigned. E. Capacity Building and Technical Support Identify capacity gaps among GBV caseworkers, volunteers and community-based structures. Organize and facilitate training, orientation, mentoring and supportive supervision on GBV guiding principles, survivor-centered case management, safe identification and referral, PSEA and confidentiality. Provide regular technical coaching to caseworkers and volunteers to improve service quality and adherence to established standards. Support the development and implementation of community-based GBV prevention and awareness plans. Document capacity-building activities, lessons learned and recommendations for continuous improvement. F. Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Reporting Develop activity plans, monthly work plans and implementation schedules in line with the approved project work plan and log frame. Monitor GBV activity implementation against agreed targets, indicators, quality standards and timelines. Maintain accurate, complete and confidential GBV service records and non-identifying statistical data. Prepare and submit timely weekly, monthly, quarterly and other required narrative and statistical reports. Monitor service delivery trends, identify implementation gaps and recommend corrective actions. Ensure accountability to affected populations through safe feedback and complaints mechanisms. Support assessments, monitoring visits, project reviews, evaluations and donor reporting processes. Document good practices, challenges, success stories and lessons learned without compromising survivor confidentiality. G. Safeguarding, PSEA and Compliance Ensure strict adherence to DANFE's Code of Conduct, PSEA policy, safeguarding standards and relevant humanitarian principles. Promote a zero-tolerance approach to sexual exploitation, abuse, harassment and discrimination. Ensure that staff and volunteers understand their safeguarding and reporting responsibilities. Identify and report safeguarding concerns through established organizational reporting mechanisms. Ensure that all activities uphold the principles of safety, dignity, non-discrimination, confidentiality and do-no-harm. Perform other relevant duties assigned by the immediate supervisor in line with the position's responsibilities.",
